quran[22]{c,v,t}:
  54,50,And Our command is nothing but a single (word) like the twinkling of an eye.
  54,51,"Indeed, We have destroyed the likes of you. So, is there anyone who will be mindful?"
  54,52,Everything they have done is in the books (of deeds).
  54,53,"And every (thing), small or big, is noted (in their record)."
  54,54,"Indeed, the God-conscious shall be (rejoicing) in gardens and rivers,"
  54,55,at the Seat of Honour (or in the Worthy Abode) in the presence of the Most-Powerful Sovereign.
  55,1,"The Most-Compassionate (Lord),"
  55,2,has taught the Qur󠄕’an.
  55,3,"He created the human being,"
  55,4,(and) taught him to communicate.
  55,5,The sun and the moon are (rotating) in calculated courses.
  55,6,The stars (or the herbs spread over the earth) and the trees bow down (in submission).
  55,7,"As for the heavens, He raised them high (by expanding them from all sides). And He set up the balance (to maintain their existence and rotation)."
  55,8,So that you may not infringe the balance.
  55,9,"Maintain the weights with justice, and do not shorten the balance."
  55,10,"As for the earth, He has laid it down for living creatures."
  55,11,"There are fruits in it and date palms bearing clusters,"
  55,12,and grain with husks and aromatic herbs.
  55,13,Then which of your Lord’s blessings do you both deny?
  55,14,"He created humans from dried clay sounding like pottery,"
  55,15,and He created the jinn from a smokeless flame of fire.
  55,16,Then which of your Lord’s blessings do you both deny?
